# remember — success
#
# REMEMBER exists only in the childhood-reminescence phase, so this test is the one that must NOT
# pass --skip-childhood: that flag skips the phase entirely and fills the starting kit as if it had
# run. Every other script in the suite passes it, which is why this verb had no test.
#
# The childhood is the first screen of a run and holds nothing but the memory at hand: its
# fragments, unnamed until one is looked at ("observe · a memory"), and what is made of them. No
# card, no panel, no token, nothing standing around. "Myself" holds the fragments as a container
# holds its contents, and is not drawn: it is whoever is remembering. A fragment is looked at,
# thought about, and reached for. No will is asked to look or to think here.
#
# The phase auto-succeeds by design — no plausibility check, no noetic cost, difficulty 0, so no
# dice. There is no `strategy` here and no meaningful failure case; `cli/remember/` has one script,
# deliberately. The fragment is named: --seed 42 fixes which memory comes first and what it holds.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue

# The phase opens on its own — no travel, no location. Wait for the mode rather than for idleness.
wait mode ChildhoodReminescence 60
advance 12 180
regions

# Only the memory's fragments: nothing else is on the screen to click, and no card is drawn.
expect-not ???
expect-state trees "Myself"
expect-no-state symbols click observe thing
expect-state symbols a scream
point observe "a scream"
wait 1
expect-state pointer-label ground=yellow text=observe · a memory

click observe "a scream"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
click think "a scream"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
regions

click act 0
advance 12 180

# No dice: the result is up at once.
expect SUCCESS
expect-verb remember

# Its CONTINUE moves on to the next memory, whose fragments take the first one's place. Nothing
# of the memory just remembered is carried over: the screen is the memory at hand.
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-no-state symbols "a scream"
expect-state symbols manure smelt
expect-no-state trees "a scream"
quit
